cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "ISO_SUBLOCSWITCH: pan-cancer subcellular-localization isoform switching"
abstract: >-
  A pipeline that tests whether tumours rewire receptor accessibility via
  alternative splicing, redistributing a gene's transcript output between
  transmembrane/cell-surface (TM), secreted (Sec) and intracellular (Int)
  compartments relative to matched normal tissue. Isoforms are assigned to
  compartments with DeepLoc 2.1, switches are called per cancer with satuRn on
  per-gene localization buckets, and results are aggregated across 14 TCGA
  cancer types for cross-cancer recurrence analysis.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Herranz
    given-names: Javier
    email: javier.herranz@sund.ku.dk
keywords:
  - alternative splicing
  - isoform switching
  - subcellular localization
  - immune escape
  - pan-cancer
  - TCGA
  - satuRn
  - differential transcript usage
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/JavierHdCKU/ISO_SUBLOCSWITCH"
